{"name":"Mountain Main","hex":"#8db8d0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mountain","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An elevation of land of considerable dimensions rising more or less abruptly, forming a conspicuous figure in the landscape, usually having a small extent of surface at its summit. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Something very large in size or quantity; a huge amount; a great heap."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mountain"},{"term":"main","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of chief or leading importance; prime, principal. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Chief, most important, or principal in extent, size, or strength; consisting of the largest part."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Exceedingly, extremely, greatly, mightily, very, very much."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/main"}],"entries":[{"title":"Main (river)","blocks":[{"text":"The Main is a river in central Germany. It is the longest tributary of the Rhine, one of the major European rivers. It rises as the White Main in the Fichtel Mountains of northeastern Bavaria and flows west for 525 kilometres (326 mi) to meet the Rhine below Rüsselsheim, Hesse. The cities of Mainz and Wiesbaden are close to the confluence."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/W%C3%BCrzburg_L%C3%B6wenbr%C3%BCcke.jpg/330px-W%C3%BCrzburg_L%C3%B6wenbr%C3%BCcke.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Main_(river)","wikidata":"Q1670"},{"title":"Mountain","blocks":[{"text":"A mountain is an elevated portion of the surface of a planet, generally with steep sides that show significant exposed bedrock. Although there are no universally accepted definitions, a mountain is usually considered higher than a hill. By definition, mountains are often thought of as being a landform which is higher than 2,000 feet (610 m). It may either have a limited summit area or be a smaller plateau with high elevation and steep sides. A few mountains are isolated summits, but most occur in mountain ranges."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Everest_North_Face_toward_Base_Camp_Tibet_Luca_Galuzzi_2006.jpg/330px-Everest_North_Face_toward_Base_Camp_Tibet_Luca_Galuzzi_2006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mountain","wikidata":"Q8502"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Main-Karte-160710.jpg/500px-Main-Karte-160710.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Main-Karte-160710.jpg/1280px-Main-Karte-160710.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Main-Karte-160710.jpg/500px-Main-Karte-160710.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMain-Karte-160710.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Verlaufskarte_Main.gif/500px-Verlaufskarte_Main.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Verlaufskarte_Main.gif/1280px-Verlaufskarte_Main.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Verlaufskarte_Main.gif/500px-Verlaufskarte_Main.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dams along the Main","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVerlaufskarte_Main.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Bassin_du_Main.png/500px-Bassin_du_Main.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conte